1
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,560
Why you?

3
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,800
Zhao Heng got stuck in a meeting.

4
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:57,560
The documents are too important.
I feel better picking them up myself.

5
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:58,880
Go get them for me.

6
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,720
Me?

7
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,120
Take my advice.

8
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,840
She'll be back in a few months
after she has the baby.

9
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:10,320
And when she comes back,
she'll still be above you.

10
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,600
It's better to make peace
than to hold a grudge.

11
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,720
I wasn't around when you took leave.

12
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,720
You're my mentor.
I thought I'd come to see you.

13
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:22,000
If your expression were more sincere,
I might actually believe you.

14
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,240
I'm not here to kick you
while you're down.

15
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,200
I don't care. Business is business.

16
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,320
Everything's here. Count them.

17
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,480
Seems like we're missing
one database key USB drive.

18
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,640
Wait here. I'll get it.

19
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:16,960
Zhiwen,

20
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,480
I dropped something in the couch cushions.

21
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,840
Can you get it for me?

22
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:22,680
I'm talking to you.

23
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,880
Coming. Let me finish this round.

24
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,640
My colleague is waiting at the door.

25
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,600
Just get it for me.
Get it and make her leave.

26
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,560
Stop rushing me!

27
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,080
I said I'll go after this round.

28
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,600
Fine. I'll wait.

29
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,800
Help me when you're done.

30
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,840
Are you crazy?

31
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:09,800
I am crazy!

32
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,000
Get away!

33
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,200
- Are you okay?
- Don't touch me.

34
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:24,840
Are you alright?

35
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,080
Let… Let me help you up.

36
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,720
What are you doing? Come help!

37
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,400
Hurry up. The floor is cold.

38
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:38,640
You're always like this. A little bump
and you act like you're dying.

39
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:43,280
Are you okay?

40
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,160
Don't worry. She's fine.

41
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,760
I'm used to it.

42
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,920
You…

43
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,920
I'll call an ambulance.

44
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,960
Ms. Lin, hang in there.

45
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,920
NOTICE OF SURGERY

46
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,760
FETAL HEARTBEAT NO LONGER DETECTABLE

47
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:46,160
I've already taken care
of the paperwork. The baby?

48
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,000
How's the baby?

49
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,120
Tell me.

50
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,120
Zhiwen.

51
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:57,960
The baby…

52
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:05,400
I'm sorry.

53
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,000
It's all my fault.

54
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,560
I'm the worst.

55
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,120
I…

56
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,120
It's okay.

57
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,920
I know you didn't mean it.

58
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,920
FIVE MINUTES AGO

59
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:37,880
Thanks.

60
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,080
It's alright.

61
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,440
I owe you one.

62
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:47,360
It's got nothing to do with you.
I made my own choices.

63
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,160
Back at your place just now…

64
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,960
Are you done yet?

65
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,880
Don't go too far!

66
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:00,920
What is wrong with you?

67
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
So clumsy. Falling on flat ground?

68
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,200
Don't worry.

69
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,680
We don't have cameras at home.

70
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,640
He fell on his own.

71
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,160
But thank you.

72
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,240
And

73
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,240
for everything I did to you before,

74
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,320
I'm sorry.

75
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,520
I don't remember
anything that happened before.

76
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,360
Alright.

77
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,640
Then I don't remember either.

78
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,720
Is there anything else you need?

79
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:34,520
Don't move.

80
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:53,400
It's all my fault.

81
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,200
I was too reckless.

82
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,360
I used too much force.

83
00:07:57,960 --> 00:08:00,120
I really didn't know you were hurt.

84
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,520
I've been the one at fault before.

85
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,720
I didn't consider your feelings.

86
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:08,240
Ms. Huang, this recording
proves at least three things.

87
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,840
First,

88
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,560
Jiang Zhiwen had been
indifferent to me for a long time

89
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,280
before my delivery.

90
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,280
Jiang Zhiwen, don't leave!
Come back here and explain yourself!

91
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,760
Are you trying to drive me
to divorce you with this cold treatment?

92
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:20,760
Don't keep using divorce as a weapon.

93
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:27,440
Second, the main cause of my miscarriage

94
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,880
was him pushing me down in anger.

95
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:31,880
Third,

96
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:34,559
the money he transferred
to his parents for the apartment

97
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,960
was a loan, not a gift.

98
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:41,080
You didn't even discuss it with me
before lending that much money to someone?

99
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:42,720
Someone?

100
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,480
They're my parents!

101
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,000
You have a very clear head,

102
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:49,240
but I suggest you wait
until you've fully recovered

103
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,320
before pursuing these matters.

104
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:55,400
Ms. Huang, you have to believe me.

105
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,320
I'm clearer-headed now
than I've ever been.

106
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:03,280
I will never regret this divorce.

107
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,640
Oh my, she really said that?

108
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,040
Yeah.

109
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,720
From the moment she came out of surgery,

110
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,040
it was like she turned back

111
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,400
into the Ms. Lin I knew
when I first joined the company.

112
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:19,000
Sound logic, clear purpose,
sharp thinking, and decisive action.

113
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:23,320
You seem to be feeling sympathy for her
because of her pain.

114
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:28,640
I just think it's hard to truly know

115
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,400
what's going on in someone's life
behind the scenes.

116
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:33,400
And at that moment, only I could help her.

117
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,960
You would've done the same.

118
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,360
You know what?
I used to think induced labor

119
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,640
was like what they show on TV.

120
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:41,920
You get anesthesia and wake up fine.

121
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,280
But it's not like that at all.

122
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:47,280
<i>Even with a pain pump,</i>
<i>you still throw up bile</i>

123
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:49,080
<i>from the dizziness and nausea.</i>

124
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,480
<i>And after the procedure,</i>

125
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:53,920
<i>someone has to press hard on your belly</i>
<i>to clear everything out.</i>

126
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:55,960
<i>Lin Long is really tough.</i>

127
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,080
<i>She didn't make a sound</i>
<i>the whole way to the hospital.</i>

128
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:02,000
<i>But I could hear her crying</i>
<i>from outside the door.</i>

129
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,240
No, not crying. She was wailing.

130
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,720
Okay. Stop saying that.

131
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,000
Let's talk about something else.

132
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,640
When are you closing
the Ande Energy project?

133
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,320
- Probably this week.
- Congratulations.

134
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,120
You have to treat everyone to a meal.

135
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,040
Can we do it after I get back
from Macao, China?

136
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:23,840
What's there to congratulate?

137
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:27,120
My dad doesn't even care
about this little deal.

138
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:29,560
What does your dad have to do with it?

139
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:32,080
This is the first contract
that you won on your own merit.

140
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,240
We can't control
whether others value it or not,

141
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,160
but we should still celebrate ourselves.

142
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,000
Makes sense.

143
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,960
Aren't you working
on the Bolo Culture project?

144
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,160
Why are you going to Macao, China?

145
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:45,520
Bolo Culture is expanding
their IP overseas.

146
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:48,000
They're negotiating with a company there
about the European market.

147
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,760
Plus,

148
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,360
I have some personal business.

149
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,840
Personal business?

150
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:09,440
Adjust your stride.
Control your breathing.

151
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:12,360
Exercise is the best way
to reset your energy.

152
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:16,800
Men usually talk a better game
than they can actually deliver.

153
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,520
Let's race the 4x10-meter shuttle run.

154
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,800
I give up.

155
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,840
Oh,

156
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,320
send me your flight number
to Macao, China.

157
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,120
I'll upgrade your seat.

158
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,520
It's free. Courtesy of Tianhe.

159
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,680
I need to brief you

160
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,400
on the Digital Finance Forum
while we're on the plane.

161
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,880
If you're in economy,
how am I supposed to do that?

162
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,680
Even though the forum
is in Macao, China, too,

163
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,120
if I come to you on a work trip,

164
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,840
won't it look like
I'm using company resources?

165
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:05,960
What if people gossip?

166
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,400
You're not attending the whole forum.

167
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:09,840
It's completely normal
to bring a date to a party.

168
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,040
If you can't manage this much,

169
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,520
how are you going to be my right hand?

170
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,200
Remember to bring a black dress.

171
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:19,400
Safe and foolproof for business occasions.

172
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:25,720
MACAO, CHINA

173
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,400
Is this the kind of black dress you meant?

174
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,800
Nice.

175
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,080
Where did you get this outfit?

176
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,120
Pretty fresh and elegant.

177
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,840
According to the invitation,
the dress code

178
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,280
is business formal.

179
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,640
I don't know much about this,
so I looked it up online.

180
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:48,200
The blogger says for business formal,
guys need black ties,

181
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,120
and women need knee-length dresses,

182
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,680
fancy jewelry, and evening clutches.

183
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:55,840
So I rushed to rent
the dress and necklace.

184
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,800
I put down a credit card as a deposit,
and it wasn't cheap.

185
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:01,840
You know what?
That blogger was pretty spot on.

186
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,840
But for an occasion like today,

187
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,080
we usually dress a bit more casually.

188
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,000
Especially in the tech industry.

189
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,600
Otherwise, it looks like
you're trying too hard.

190
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:11,600
You look great.

191
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:12,880
Just a little overdone.

192
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:20,960
I see.

193
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:28,800
Perfect.

194
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:41,520
GOLDEN BAY AREA DIGITAL FINANCE
AND INDUSTRY EMPOWERMENT SUMMIT

195
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:15,040
Do you go to these cocktail parties often?

196
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,880
I noticed you guys
just exchanged simple greetings

197
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,640
and chatted about diving and kayaking.

198
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:24,160
How does that kind of
casual acquaintance help with work?

199
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,840
For a client,

200
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:28,440
they instinctively trust
that someone with higher income

201
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:31,040
understands their investment needs
and financial risks better.

202
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,000
Same goes for business partnerships.

203
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,320
Most deals are built on trust,

204
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,760
not capability.

205
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:39,760
And trust takes time
and repeated interactions to build.

206
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,760
Once you get used to this circle,

207
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,320
opportunities will naturally
open up for you.

208
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,680
Get used to this circle?

209
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,160
Are you planning to do
digital asset projects in the future?

210
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:53,440
You know why the consulting industry
has been shrinking these past few years,

211
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:57,400
yet C&C still manages to beat out
high-and-mighty foreign firms like yours?

212
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,640
Because those old-school consulting tricks
are all over the internet now.

213
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:07,080
And I've always insisted on staying close
to the front lines of real industries.

214
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:10,400
That way, I can offer clients
strategic advice with real substance.

215
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:14,200
Otherwise, even if we fool
some clueless rich folks now,

216
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:16,920
the times will eventually leave us behind.

217
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:22,240
So that's why you briefly
left Boen to work at P&J?

218
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:25,760
Actually, even though
P&J is an FMCG giant,

219
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,360
their consulting budget
has been shrinking year after year.

220
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:33,800
Just because these emerging
tech companies spend big,

221
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,000
you…

222
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,280
What is a consultant's mission?

223
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,720
To improve the world's
management standards?

224
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:39,760
No.

225
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,160
It's to get orders.

226
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,320
Orders are what matter.

227
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,600
Consultants can't know every industry.

228
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:48,840
Even a genius can only master
three to four business domains at most.

229
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,840
When choosing industries,

230
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,880
you have to find ones
with money and orders.

231
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:57,480
I've done internships in FMCG,
logistics, and manufacturing.

232
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:58,760
You want the truth?

233
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:02,320
If your first project
wasn't an internet unicorn

234
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,320
like Bolo Culture,

235
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,720
you wouldn't be standing here.

236
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,960
Ever since the interview,
every time you talk about work,

237
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:15,720
your style is brutally direct.

238
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,880
Playing with kids
and training subordinates

239
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,800
are completely different things.

240
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,480
Welcome to the real world.

241
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,360
You brought your little junior here?

242
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:57,320
See? She's already overwhelmed.

243
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,240
We're not at the same company,
and we don't get much time together.

244
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:05,319
I brought her here
to see if she's our kind of person.

245
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:08,079
She's a blank slate right now.

246
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,520
It's good for you to show her
more of the world.

247
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,560
Like…

248
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,720
Look.

249
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,600
An old friend of mine just showed up.

250
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,960
Come with me to say hi.

251
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:36,440
Okay.

252
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,800
How's your current project going?

253
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,440
- Long time no see.
- Xinzhi.

254
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,440
- You're here too?
- You're here too.

255
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,600
- What a coincidence.
- Small world.

256
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,040
Xu Chi, let me introduce you to a legend.

257
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:49,040
He's my former mentor,
Wen Ruosen, a partner at Boen.

258
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:51,360
Hello. I'm Xu Chi.

259
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,680
Nice to meet you, Miss Xu.

260
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,280
Is Miss Xu in consulting?

261
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,440
- Yes.
- Let me warn you.

262
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:57,880
Be careful with this guy.
He's got a silver tongue.

263
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:59,760
Don't fall for his tricks.

264
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,440
Actually, I've already left the industry.

265
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,640
I'm incubating my own projects now.

266
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,320
Oh, let me introduce you.

267
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,600
This is the CEO
of Benyuan Digital Collectibles.

268
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,920
Benyuan is the largest

269
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,360
digital collectibles platform
in Hong Kong, China.

270
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:13,640
I know.

271
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,800
I actually collected
a Yifubao red-envelope skin featuring

272
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,040
the Northern Wei Grottoes a few days ago.

273
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,480
I'm quite interested in this area.

274
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:19,520
I would love to learn more.

275
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:26,280
Hello. I'm Tang Yisheng, Tommy.

276
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,680
Sorry. My Mandarin isn't very good.

277
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:31,000
My Cantonese isn't all that good either.

278
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:32,920
We can chat more in the future.

279
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,840
Sure. Come on. Cheers.

280
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,160
- Come on.
- Cheers.

281
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,360
- Cheers.
- Come on.

282
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,480
Pleasure.

283
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,400
Tired?

284
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,440
Not really.

285
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,880
I noted down the key points

286
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,320
from Wen Ruosen
and Mr. Tang's private conversation

287
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,440
in Cantonese.

288
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,320
I'm sending it to you in case I forget.

289
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,720
Wen Ruosen has a lot of connections
in the art world.

290
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,560
He runs a digital collectibles agency,

291
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:24,480
kind of like a gallery,
called Yuanzhou Gallery.

292
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:27,520
They want to partner with Mr. Tang's
collectibles platform in Hong Kong, China.

293
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,320
You speak Cantonese?

294
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,000
My high school teacher,

295
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:35,120
who looked after me growing up,
is from Guangdong.

296
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:38,720
Secretly gathering business intelligence?

297
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:41,120
Nice one, Chi.

298
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,800
Nothing much.

299
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,840
You were just talking
about digital assets nonstop,

300
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,320
and then you zeroed in
on those two digital collectibles.

301
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,240
Your eyes were darting around
when you looked at Mr. Wen.

302
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:53,280
Of course, I had to figure out
what I could do for you.

303
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,800
Take a look. Is this useful?

304
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,120
Decent.

305
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,920
So,

306
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,720
what did you do here all night?

307
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:03,840
I also organized
all the new business cards you received.

308
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,280
I jotted down notes

309
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:07,040
on key conversation points
and general profiles of each person.

310
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,200
I'll export them tonight
and send them to you.

311
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:13,080
And I heard a lot of people talking
about dual carbon and green finance today.

312
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,520
I think it's going to be a big trend.

313
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,960
When I get back,
I'll do more research on that.

314
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:19,560
You can maintain
such sharp business instincts

315
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:22,000
in a social setting like this.

316
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:23,800
There are not many girls like you around.

317
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:26,240
I'm not here to see the world.

318
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:29,360
I just want to become your trusted protege

319
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,480
as quickly as possible.

320
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,640
So, Master?

321
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,640
Did I do okay today?

322
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:39,440
Not quite yet.

323
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:41,960
What did I miss?

324
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,520
You're not relaxed enough.

325
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,440
You've been holding that glass all day.

326
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:46,680
Barely touched it.

327
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:50,080
You told me not to drink at these events.

328
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,480
Besides,

329
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:55,400
I am here.

330
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,280
We're too busy at work.

331
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:11,880
Sometimes,

332
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,400
you really should learn from me

333
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:16,520
how to balance work and life.

334
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,200
Here we go again.

335
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:58,200
The research is about 60% complete.

336
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:00,520
Next up are the key interviews
and modeling.

337
00:23:00,600 --> 00:23:03,920
Once those are done,
consultants like Cindy

338
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,840
will each take charge
of analyzing one module.

339
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:08,120
Then we get to the main event
of strategic consulting.

340
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,920
The process doesn't matter.

341
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:10,920
I only care about the results.

342
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,400
By the way,

343
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:14,800
I meant to ask you last time.

344
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:17,280
Why isn't Lin Long
on this consulting team?

345
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:20,480
Did she actually take my advice
and go on maternity leave?

346
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:24,880
What's wrong?

347
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,320
Something happened?

348
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,400
Is it about the baby?

349
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,920
She really went through it.

350
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,480
How is she doing lately?

351
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,760
Did you see her?

352
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,520
She's okay. She's recovering.

353
00:23:57,680 --> 00:23:59,000
She's been through a lot lately.

354
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,040
You seem to be doing
pretty well for yourself, though.

355
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,400
Your boyfriend is quite handsome.

356
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:13,360
He's not my boyfriend.
You've got it wrong.

357
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,280
I get it.

358
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:16,080
Girls are hard to read.

359
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,560
- No… No.
- Well, good luck then.

360
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:18,480
Hope you lock it down soon.

361
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,680
He's really not my boyfriend.
He's my senior.

362
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:21,760
Senior?

363
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:26,200
You and your senior
were posing like this in the background?

364
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:29,160
Next time, if you have
something like this…

365
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:31,760
Mr. Shen, let's get back to work.

366
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:33,960
Okay.

367
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:35,320
I'll send you that photo later.

368
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,440
You can run your own model.

369
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:38,520
Check what the odds are
for the two of you.

370
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:41,320
- Make a prediction.
- Mr. Shen…

371
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:51,600
<i>You told me not to drink at these events.</i>

372
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:54,760
I told you not to drink recklessly.

373
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:56,040
Besides,

374
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:57,240
I am here.

375
00:24:58,800 --> 00:24:59,840
I'm fine.

376
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:03,440
Let me recite it for you. Three point
one four one five nine two six

377
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:05,080
- three two three eight four six two…
- Stop reciting.

378
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:07,000
Do it in the car.

379
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,680
SAVE IMAGE

380
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:03,640
Here's the research
on those investment funds you asked for.

381
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,680
I've done it
on my personal computer as you requested.

382
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:09,160
Right. Remember,
always keep the work I give you

383
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,440
physically separate from Maxmise files.

384
00:26:11,520 --> 00:26:12,960
No problem.

385
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:15,600
Even on my personal computer,
I've set up separate encryption.

386
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:17,960
Oh, and one more thing.

387
00:26:18,040 --> 00:26:19,560
Some of the information

388
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,440
on the Yuanke Factory
contact is not public.

389
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:23,400
I have a colleague
I'm close with named Zhao Heng.

390
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:26,400
He used to be that person's assistant
during his internship.

391
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,840
So I asked him to help.

392
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:30,120
Got it.

393
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,720
I'll go through it when I get back.

394
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:32,840
Okay.

395
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,560
How are you holding up?

396
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:36,680
Juggling work on both sides lately.

397
00:26:37,280 --> 00:26:38,400
Can you handle it?

398
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:43,080
Barely.

399
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:45,680
But I have to earn every penny
of the salary you pay me.

400
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:47,680
Salary?

401
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:48,680
It's just a red envelope.

402
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:52,160
I'm just teaching you
some Spanish on the side,

403
00:26:52,240 --> 00:26:53,200
not hiring you for a part-time job.

404
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:59,120
Hello. Thanks. Bye.

405
00:26:59,800 --> 00:27:00,640
Don't worry.

406
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:02,600
That's what I tell people too.

407
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:10,920
Hey, Ms. Sha.

408
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:13,880
Yes.

409
00:27:13,960 --> 00:27:15,920
It's on my phone. I'll send it right away.

410
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,080
You scumbag!

411
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:08,480
If you never loved me,
why didn't you tell me sooner?

412
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:10,480
I'm asking you a question!

413
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:13,040
Why did you keep stringing me along
and giving me false hope?

414
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,920
Why aren't TV crews camped out here?

415
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:18,200
I mean, look at this place.

416
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:22,120
Cheesy romance. Detective thrillers.
Rags to riches and riches to rags.

417
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:24,560
So much material.

418
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:27,640
What's wrong?

419
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:30,880
Nothing. You can go.

420
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:38,160
I'm off.

421
00:28:46,080 --> 00:28:47,360
<i>I forgot to give you a few documents.</i>

422
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:49,320
<i>The classification is too high.</i>
<i>Can't email them.</i>

423
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,640
<i>Can you drop by my place</i>
<i>after work to pick them up?</i>

424
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,480
YE XINZHI

425
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:54,680
<i>Is 10:45 okay?</i>

426
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:55,600
XU CHI

427
00:28:55,680 --> 00:28:56,920
<i>Okay.</i>

428
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:06,280
SONGFENG RESTAURANT

429
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:25,920
That was fast.
I thought it was room service.

430
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:26,880
Come in. I'll go get them.

431
00:29:28,520 --> 00:29:29,680
- I…
- It's fine.

432
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:30,920
No need to change shoes.

433
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,920
You haven't eaten this late?

434
00:29:44,440 --> 00:29:46,320
Where's the potted plant I bought you?

435
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:01,880
The document and USB drive are all here.
Thanks for coming all this way.

436
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:04,800
No worries.

437
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:07,320
Thanks. Sorry to make
you come all this way at this hour.

438
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:12,040
I'm off.

439
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,360
Here is the document.
Here's the USB drive.

440
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:46,760
Thanks for coming all this way.

441
00:31:21,600 --> 00:31:22,920
Xu Chi.

442
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,680
You're an idiot!

443
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:29,880
He definitely wanted you to see that.

444
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:33,640
What are you looking at?

445
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:36,320
I'm talking about you.

446
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:39,800
You've been caught red-handed.

447
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:42,440
Who are you?

448
00:31:42,520 --> 00:31:45,400
What right do you have to overthink this?

449
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:47,800
Got humiliated, didn't you?

450
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:49,400
Does it hurt?

451
00:31:50,480 --> 00:31:51,560
So stupid!

452
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,640
Hey, neighbor! Are you okay?

453
00:31:57,720 --> 00:31:58,880
I'm fine!

454
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:00,640
Sorry!

455
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:04,760
So stupid!

456
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:11,160
So cruel.

457
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:16,680
If I hadn't known you for years,

458
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:19,040
I wouldn't have helped you
with something this cruel.

459
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:22,240
What are you doing,
making that poor girl so upset?

460
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:26,720
Better she's heartbroken now
than later, right?

461
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:28,760
Thank you for today.

462
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:31,880
I don't know who else
I could've asked for this favor.

463
00:32:34,320 --> 00:32:35,800
Lucky I happened to come back
to the country recently.

464
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:37,600
But

465
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:39,640
Xiaoyezi,

466
00:32:39,720 --> 00:32:41,320
you've been single for so long.

467
00:32:41,400 --> 00:32:43,560
Maybe you could consider…

468
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:44,840
I've tried before.

469
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:47,200
But whenever I think
of what happened before,

470
00:32:47,720 --> 00:32:49,000
I can't bring myself to do it again.

471
00:32:50,360 --> 00:32:51,640
I'm too busy.

472
00:32:52,280 --> 00:32:53,840
I don't have the energy left to love.

473
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:58,400
So some sparks
are better snuffed out early.

474
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:25,520
Stay calm.

475
00:33:26,720 --> 00:33:28,200
The fact that he did that

476
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,600
means there's still hope.

477
00:33:31,120 --> 00:33:32,280
Otherwise,

478
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:35,080
he would've just quietly cut you loose.

479
00:33:40,200 --> 00:33:41,400
So wake up now

480
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:46,720
while he's still giving you a chance.
Stop saving random photos.

481
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:48,520
I need to go to the airport.

482
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:53,080
Xiaoyezi. Remember to be kind
to yourself and to others.

483
00:33:54,840 --> 00:33:55,760
Bye.

484
00:33:56,440 --> 00:33:57,480
Thanks.

485
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:07,280
Xu Chi.

486
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:09,520
From now on, you focus only on your work.

487
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:13,159
Your goals are your career
and your apartment, not men.

488
00:34:19,239 --> 00:34:20,760
DELETE

489
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:23,000
CONFIRM DELETE SELECTED FILES
FROM LOCAL DRIVE? CANCEL / CONFIRM

490
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:25,840
CONFIRM

491
00:35:11,840 --> 00:35:12,880
<i>Still not awake?</i>

492
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:14,720
<i>Or did you not sleep at all?</i>

493
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,440
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

494
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:20,440
<i>But it's for the best for both of us.</i>

495
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:29,280
Morning.

496
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:36,960
A sweet night, right?

497
00:35:37,040 --> 00:35:39,080
Can't believe you're up so early.
Impressive.

498
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:40,960
Take your time running, sir.

499
00:35:41,040 --> 00:35:42,640
I have already done two laps.

500
00:35:42,720 --> 00:35:44,120
I'm heading up.

501
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:29,360
It's okay.

502
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:32,200
You did great just now.

503
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,760
Very natural.

504
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:51,000
A sweet night, right?

505
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,720
Can't believe you're up so early.
Impressive.

506
00:36:53,560 --> 00:36:54,920
"Can't believe you're up so early."

507
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:56,560
Take your time running, sir.

508
00:36:56,640 --> 00:36:58,200
I have already done two laps.

509
00:36:58,280 --> 00:36:59,320
"Sir"?

510
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:03,840
After all that,

511
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,840
I was the one overthinking it.

512
00:37:26,960 --> 00:37:28,440
You're pretty free today.

513
00:37:29,680 --> 00:37:31,560
Thought you wouldn't
show up at the office.

514
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:36,120
The interviews with Bolo Culture are done,

515
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:37,680
and the initial model is built.

516
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:39,360
Cindy and the others are reviewing it.

517
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:40,760
I'm still new.

518
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:43,680
I've done what I can.

519
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:46,720
Just waiting for them
to reassign tasks now.

520
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:49,440
Bored?

521
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:52,840
A little.

522
00:37:54,200 --> 00:37:57,760
I was so pumped
when I landed this project.

523
00:37:57,840 --> 00:38:00,920
Felt like I was ready
to go all in for a year.

524
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:05,160
Now, not even a third of the way in,
I'm already running out of steam.

525
00:38:05,240 --> 00:38:07,160
Not challenging enough?

526
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:10,240
Consulting is a lot like art.

527
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:13,840
We're all trying to shape something raw
into something refined.

528
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:17,000
What consultants enjoy
is the creative process.

529
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:19,520
You never know
how brilliant the result will be

530
00:38:19,600 --> 00:38:21,040
until you put down the final stroke.

531
00:38:22,080 --> 00:38:24,960
Bolo Culture just wants to use you
to get rid of people they don't want.

532
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:28,520
So what if your proposal is flashy?

533
00:38:28,600 --> 00:38:30,000
You already know the ending.
There's no suspense.

534
00:38:30,680 --> 00:38:31,800
How do you know so much?

535
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:36,360
I interned at Beisen's New York office
my sophomore year.

536
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:39,720
I've led more projects
than the number of men you've dated.

537
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:42,920
I've only had one ex-boyfriend. Thanks.

538
00:38:45,360 --> 00:38:46,560
Just one?

539
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:48,120
I don't believe you.

540
00:38:50,240 --> 00:38:51,880
You dare let me check your phone?

541
00:38:53,480 --> 00:38:54,600
Check it then.

542
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:55,960
Three, two, one.

543
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:58,080
That confident?

544
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:09,200
You slipped up.

545
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:12,160
Recently deleted. Why did you delete it?

546
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:13,760
Give it to me.

547
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:14,720
- Why did you delete it?
- Give it…

548
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:16,760
Guilty?

549
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:21,520
Who's this guy?

550
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:26,760
Isn't that the poser?

551
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:31,320
I knew there was something
between you two.

552
00:39:31,400 --> 00:39:32,920
There's nothing between us.

553
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:36,040
We're just master and protege.

554
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:39,240
What is this, a TV drama?
Master and protege?

555
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:40,440
Let me tell you.

556
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:44,560
You're just a junior analyst at Maxmise.
He's a partner at C&C.

557
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:45,760
You two are this close.

558
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:47,680
You should be thankful
no one's reporting you

559
00:39:47,760 --> 00:39:48,800
for corporate espionage.

560
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:50,600
I know compliance. I…

561
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:53,520
He's just teaching me Spanish.

562
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,520
That's even worse.

563
00:39:56,600 --> 00:39:58,720
He's a handsome,
wealthy industry big shot.

564
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:01,040
If he didn't want something from you,

565
00:40:01,120 --> 00:40:02,680
why would he be so nice

566
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:05,440
as to teach you Spanish?

567
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:09,560
You think you're some web novel heroine
who finds cheat codes everywhere?

568
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:12,920
What could he possibly want from me?

569
00:40:15,160 --> 00:40:16,880
You're overthinking it.

570
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:19,320
Just overthinking it.

571
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:23,120
Overthinking it.

572
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,040
What's going on?

573
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:29,920
Wait, wait.

574
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:33,120
What did I say?
